\caption{Operator content and scalar feedback. Archived classical circuit-ensemble calculations, seed 20240603 and 2,000 samples per point. (a) Scalar-gradient variance $\operatorname{Var}(g)$ decreases with qubit number $n$. (b) The normalised operator-gradient fraction $r_{\rm op}=\|A\|_{\rm HS}^2/\|O\|_{\rm HS}^2$ remains near one half. Bars are archived sample standard deviations, not confidence intervals. The local and global observable ensembles nearly coincide in this experiment. The comparison isolates the scalar-projection mechanism. Measuring the operator content remains a separate resource cost.}
