\caption{Choose an omitted direction by its value, not only its amplitude. Each method adds one direction from the same pool in the archived residual prototype. Coupling $\lambda$ and retained-space energy error $E_P-E_0$ use the model's dimensionless units. Raw residual amplitude favours a high-gap channel. The implemented amplitude-over-gap rule selects a more useful low-gap channel and leaves a smaller error. The curves are exact dense-state calculations for the displayed Hamiltonian and two-candidate pool.}
\label{fig:dd-gap-selection}
