\paragraph{Why the relational questions fail.}
A source-level audit separates two mechanisms. One development question asks how many projects a person has led or is currently leading. All four required turns are present among the 505 source records, but whole-question embedding retrieval ranks them 63rd, 111th, 208th and 228th. Combining parent and child queries changes those ranks to 66th, 112th, 207th and 241st. Neither the 2,000- nor the 4,000-token context contains the required evidence. The data exists. What is missing is an effective translation from the question to a join over project identities, leadership roles and time, followed by a count. A parent embedding alone does not supply that operation.

A purchase-order question fails differently. Its two support records rank first and ninth under the whole question, and first and seventeenth after merging. Both enter the 2,000-token context, but a first-fit packing rule admits earlier, larger groups at 4,000 tokens and displaces a needed later record. More nominal space can therefore produce a worse evidence set. This is a packing defect, distinguishable from failure to encode a relation during ingestion.

Doubling the evidence budget in the follow-up improves all three methods and helps memory on multi-session questions. Some contexts nevertheless lose previously selected evidence when the budget grows. The audit therefore identifies two different improvements: represent the missing relations explicitly and make evidence packing preserve useful support as capacity increases.

The next implementation should therefore make the relation-bearing part of ingestion explicit. Source-backed entity identities, aliases, roles, events and temporal qualifiers would give a query something on which to execute a join, count or ordering operation. The test is whether this improves held-out relational answers at a fixed evidence budget, with each answer still traceable to its records. A separate branch-preserving packing test should require that enlarging the budget does not discard already selected support. These proposals turn the audit into tests of relation extraction, query execution and evidence packing.

The exact-coordinate campaign and the language campaign now fit together. The former gives an exact composable construction and a measured advantage over scans on the displayed query family. The latter shows the cost of not yet extracting or accessing the right relation reliably. Together they make memory a practical development target: retain the structure that answers the question, preserve its witnesses, and measure the failures that tell us what to ingest next.\footnote{\href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=development\%2Fmemory-implementation-tests-and-ingestion-20261015.md&expected_sha256=58d09f2816925284a5474927252c8669d00a339c2b42113fd2d762e5e017412c&owner=writing-artifact&artifact_id=ART-bd22fdbeb3be435da142b3a767f23e00}{Memory implementation, exact test counts and source-level relational failure analysis}. \href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=reading\%2Fcontinuous-pipeline-memory-checkpoint-20261015.md&expected_sha256=9d30d357f5db2349f25728866a378c50fbce18d8e36574b3f0e6dec664c39327&owner=writing-artifact}{Original Corpus and Memory in Pieces: source interpretation, maps and campaign controls}.}

The nearest comparisons already exploit structure. GraphRAG extracts entities and relations with a language model, forms graph communities and writes multilevel community summaries. Queries map over summaries and combine intermediate answers. Its principal evidence concerns global sensemaking over large corpora, including breadth and diversity judged against vector retrieval. It is not merely a cosine index. What it does not supply is the particular operator-intertwining residual and task-error contract in Eqs.~\eqref{eq:memory-object}--\eqref{eq:memory-task-error}. Whether that additional contract helps depends on a task for which it can be evaluated.\footnote{D. Edge et al., \emph{From Local to Global: A GraphRAG Approach to Query-Focused Summarization}, \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16130}{arXiv:2404.16130}, version 2.}~\cite{Edge202448436b}

RAPTOR recursively embeds, clusters and summarises text, retaining original chunks alongside higher-level descriptions. Its main evaluated retrieval method searches across all levels rather than relying on a logarithmic tree descent. Its results therefore support the value of multiscale representational content, not an automatic routing complexity advantage. The relevant comparison keeps the reader, context budget and evaluator fixed.\footnote{P. Sarthi et al., \emph{RAPTOR: Recursive Abstractive Processing for Tree-Organized Retrieval}, ICLR 2024, \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.18059}{arXiv:2401.18059}. \href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=reading\%2Fcontinuous-itqde-and-retrieval-comparisons-20261015.md&expected_sha256=963ef64435c0e555f4b7ed76785b232031ca88282490eaa94862b5f326900f2e&owner=writing-artifact}{Primary-source methods, controlled comparisons, indexing costs and summary-accuracy limits}.}~\cite{Sarthi2024a1f229}

Retrieval-Centric Deep Learning in Growing Nonparametric Neural Networks~\cite{Reference2026d462c2} offers another instructive connection. For a linear layer updated by gradient descent, the final weight matrix can be expressed as its initial value plus a sum of stored input and update-vector outer products. Evaluation then has an exact attention-like dual representation of the training trajectory. Its kernel extension makes the link more general, while practical approximations change the exact correspondence. The memory grows with the retained updates, so the duality itself does not provide compression. This reinforces Eigen's central question: which task-relevant part of a large history can be retained in a smaller composable object, and how do we detect when that object is no longer enough?\footnote{\href{https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.03858}{RCDL primary source, arXiv:2610.03858v1}, especially its linear-layer Eq.~(1) and nonlinear constructions in Section~3.}

The useful application is not restricted to conversational recall. Repeated relational enquiries, exception-sensitive corpus inspection and local predictive models all need a representation that preserves more than an average embedding. A memory system becomes more valuable when its answer includes a route back to the source and a meaningful account of what its compression could have missed.

\section{The backend: objects, authority and revision}
\label{section:the-backend-objects-authority-and-revision}

A memory answer needs a route back to its sources. A research result needs that route too, together with a record of the assumptions, calculations and judgements that make it usable. Someone else must be able to inspect it, change its inputs and understand what must be reconsidered. The Writing App is an integrated research environment built around that continuity. It keeps the material, the claims made about it, the work performed on it and the decisions that accept it connected. The manuscript is one view of that research state. Calculations, source passages and review are other views, with tools for moving between them.

Take the gap-aware quantum example. A calculation reports that a gap-aware enlargement sharply reduces the energy error in a specified model and candidate pool. A claim states what that comparison supports. A figure displays it, and a paragraph explains why the energy denominator helped. A reviewer may ask whether the same selection rule works on another Hamiltonian. That question needs the model, pool, selection rule and original result, together with a way to add the next calculation without losing the first.

\paragraph{An object that carries its meaning and its grounds.}
The system gives each of these objects an identity and an interface. Its detailed material may be a mathematical statement, a table, code, a source passage or a reference to a larger file. Around that material sit a readable summary, typed relationships, revision information and the operations currently allowed. We call this organising pattern a \emph{conceptric envelope}: a unit of knowledge that carries enough context to be inspected and safely used elsewhere.

Figure~\ref{fig:dd-conceptric-envelope} follows the claim in the quantum example. Its exterior says what the result concerns and how to inspect it. Inside are the statement, assumptions and exact grounds. The relationships say that a source supports a method, a calculation tests a configuration, and a figure or paragraph uses the resulting claim. Giving these relationships types makes a practical difference. A source citation supplies documentary support, while a logical premise supplies something the argument requires. A chapter contains a paragraph, while a review task depends on the version it inspected.

Two kinds of digest help here. A readable digest tells another reader or task what the object means. A content digest or revision identifies which version was used. The first makes a large collection navigable, while the second makes a later comparison exact. The app exposes these through the existing claim, source, result and Work interfaces, with each kind of object retaining the details appropriate to its job.

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/robot-run-c4d4b3872a904ec0.result/dd-conceptric-envelope.pdf}
\caption{A claim with a readable exterior. The gap-aware comparison retains its model, candidate pool and source/result links, while the containing task receives a concise account of what it can use. The action interface admits changes against the current version. Blue marks the object and its operations, teal the outward flow of observations.}
\label{fig:dd-conceptric-envelope}
\end{figure}

The direction of information is important. Here \emph{inside} means an object's detailed material and local state, and \emph{outside} means its interface and the task that contains or uses it. \emph{Reading goes in to out}: observations of the inner material become the summary or selected detail exposed to that task. A request to open a source points inward, but the information returned from it flows outward. \emph{Writing goes out to in}: an outer intention, such as revising the energy claim, is narrowed to an allowed operation on a particular inner object. Its outcome then becomes visible outside again.

This arrangement gives a task control over its level of detail. A comparison of methods may need a result summary and its conditions. Checking one number may need the precise configuration and table row. Editing a caption needs the figure's data and the current words. The system supplies bounded observations for those different purposes and provides explicit routes to further detail. Semantic selection still matters: the author or agent must ask for the material the inference needs.

\paragraph{How an AI acts through the harness.}
The \emph{harness} is the software around the model that prepares its context, exposes tools and routes their requests. It starts with the selected project, the author's question, the relevant objects and the session's role. A working author session and an independent reviewer have different available operations. A child calculation also has a declared task and a place to return its result. These boundaries make responsibility visible before an action is taken.

Suppose the AI wants to link the new calculation to the energy claim. It submits a structured request identifying both objects and the revisions it has inspected. The gateway checks the operation, the role and the project scope.~\cite{Referenceb6ad3c,Reference76a1e2} The request then reaches the \emph{owner}, the application component responsible for that kind of change. The owner checks the relevant current identities and records the admitted transition. Source editing adds its own checks on the selected manuscript, exact original passage and proposed replacement. Figure~\ref{fig:dd-ai-tool-harness} shows this route.

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/robot-run-c4d4b3872a904ec0.result/dd-ai-tool-harness.pdf}
\caption{From a model request to an inspectable result. The harness supplies task context and checks permission. The owning operation checks the current basis and records the change. The human and parent task can inspect the same outcome, judge its interpretation and request a revision. The loop keeps the proposal, action and acceptance connected.}
\label{fig:dd-ai-tool-harness}
\end{figure}

The return explains what happened and where to inspect it. For a numerical producer, that includes its inputs, execution outcome and output. For a source change, it includes the affected passage and recorded revision. If a write lands but a later recording step is interrupted, the retained source effect identifies the completed part, allowing recovery to finish the record without applying the edit twice. Recovery can therefore distinguish a committed source change from a pending record and resume the unfinished part.\footnote{The linked implementation account identifies the source-inspected recovery branches. Executed examples and their bounds are recorded separately in the evidence below.}

Scientific acceptance enters at a different point in the same route. A human or designated model reviewer judges whether the evidence supports the stated interpretation. The literature tool records that judgement alongside the observed passage and the claim version. Numerical checks test a declared calculation. Formal checks test an encoded proposition and its assumptions. The parent task brings those contributions together and records what it accepts. Each participant can inspect the basis of the decision and challenge the relevant step.

The implementation records the authored support judgement and its consumed passage separately from result currentness and completion acceptance.~\cite{Reference2075a8,Reference8e9e64,Reference603f66,Reference25a6c0}

\paragraph{What a change sets in motion.}
Now change the candidate pool used by the quantum calculation. The original result still describes its original pool. The new input gives the next calculation a different basis, and any explanation that intends to use the new result needs attention. A paragraph's wording may remain byte-for-byte unchanged while its supporting comparison has moved. This is why the system tracks a content revision separately from the currentness of its grounds.

Work records make the consequence actionable. A task stores its objective, current standing, declared prerequisites and completion evidence. Acceptance retains the exact prerequisite completions and evidence it consumed. When one of those changes, the current observation can mark that acceptance stale and identify the affected input. A new run, revised interpretation or fresh review can then restore the local chain. The scope of this propagation is the declared dependency graph. It gives the system a precise way to ask what needs reconsidering, while people and reviewers decide how the scientific account should change.

The human interface exposes the same state through manuscript, research, reference, logical-structure and Work views. The AI enters through tools that reach the same owners. A reader can open the claim, follow its result or source, inspect the proposed change and see its outcome. For repository inspection, \nolinkurl{docs/writing-source-map.md} is the entry point, with the transaction in \nolinkurl{src/laplace/writing/source_application.py}, context admission in \nolinkurl{src/laplace/writing/turn_admission.py}, and task acceptance in \nolinkurl{src/laplace/project_work.py}.\footnote{\href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=development\%2Fepistemic-envelope-harness-and-composition-20261015.md&expected_sha256=2ade627dd00d640aa370928be3f8828c595d64d1b5eba2d3024924c974eded04&owner=writing-artifact&artifact_id=ART-27a42aaacb12416cbd6dc33dc1f6dfc7}{Present-system source map, reached operations and diagram interpretation}.}

The hierarchy figure in this briefing followed that route. A supervised calculation produced the stability curves and checked their boundary against the linearised dynamics. We interpreted the result, bound it to the feedback claim, and revised the explanation and figure placement against the current source. The editor preserved the preceding text, recorded the application and rebuilt the PDF. A reader can consequently move from the displayed boundary back to the model and calculation, or forward from the claim to the passage that uses it.\footnote{\href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=development\%2Fselected-requests-memory-lawhood-hierarchy-20261016.json&expected_sha256=f7d78e24d32c106eb60ded84f714c2126a8beea42847ef1a1f485b488d360a8b&owner=writing-artifact&artifact_id=ART-3c5ca7d55de8437bbcb6aacf23ff72d7}{Exact result, source applications, build and complete rendered reading for that edition}.}

The open-systems discussion gives a useful design comparison. A scientific object's meaning depends on its context: a Hamiltonian convention, candidate pool or source version can change what its conclusion supports. Eigen retains those consequential relationships at the object's boundary, while exposing only the detail needed by the current task. When a surrounding assumption changes, the relevant consumer must be reconsidered. The boundary retains the dependencies that make a local operation safe to compose with the rest of the work.

The connection to the earlier theory is now concrete. A useful representation keeps the distinctions required by an operation and exposes the cost of losing them. For this software, those distinctions include the material, its interpretation, the authority to change it and the evidence on which a decision rests. Preserving them lets a small local operation participate in a larger research process. The same boundary can then be repeated at the level of a calculation, a manuscript section or an entire project.

\section{Research that can inspect its own results}
\label{section:research-that-can-inspect-its-own-results}

These mechanisms matter most when a result needs to be questioned rather than merely stored. Eigen's campaign on the SuperARC benchmark followed that path: an attractive score prompted closer examination of what the score measured. Its strongest scientific product was the resulting correction.

The original benchmark starts from an algorithmic-information idea: a compact executable account of data can express structure that literal reproduction does not. A program has consequences. It can be run, compared with a target and challenged on new inputs. SuperARC turns that motivation into several finite tests, including sequence reconstruction and prediction. Those are distinct tasks: reproducing a supplied finite prefix does not establish its unseen continuation.\footnote{Hern\'andez-Espinosa et al., \emph{SuperARC: a test for artificial superintelligence based on compressed modelling, recursive prediction and problem complexity}, Nature Communications 17,4885 (2026), \href{https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-73289-5}{doi:10.1038/s41467-026-73289-5}.}~\cite{HernndezEspinosa2026c672f1}

For its reconstruction score, correct answers are divided into non-print/non-ordinal, ordinal and print categories. If their fractions are $\rho_1,\rho_2,\rho_3$, the score is
\begin{equation}
 \phi=\rho_1\delta_1+0.1\rho_2\delta_2+0.01\rho_3\delta_3.
 \label{eq:superarc-score}
\end{equation}
Within each category, $\delta_k$ is a harmonic mean of $\tanh[\mathrm{nBDM}(\mathrm{target})/\mathrm{nBDM}(\mathrm{answer})]$. Normalised block decomposition complexity, nBDM, is a finite operational approximation inspired by algorithmic information theory. The category weights build a preference for generative-looking answers into the instrument. Changing an answer's category can change its contribution by a factor of ten or a hundred without changing execution correctness.

The \href{/projection/pdf?corpus=superarc&file=synthetics+papers\%2Fsuperarc\%2Fmanuscript\%2Fmain.pdf&expected_content_revision=sha256\%3Ab4166668e025815cb4e346a3c307c8efcf0e2a5b08f9e4429b5bfa29aed967a0}{Eigen SuperARC campaign (PDF)} generated answers to 100 twelve-term binary sequences using a bare arm, an iterative loop and an execute/fix comparison arm. All three recorded correct outcomes on every target under their respective checking routes. Their answer forms differed sharply: the bare arm mostly printed the sequence, while the two active arms mostly produced generative-looking expressions. Figure~\ref{fig:dd-superarc-controls} shows how those categories and the subsequent format controls affect the score.
\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/portable-run-b69220b3a27348ad.result/dd-superarc-controls.pdf}
\caption{The recorded Eigen campaign on the SuperARC reconstruction task. (a) Fractions $\rho_k$ in each correct-answer category for $N=100$ twelve-term binary targets. All arms recorded correct outcomes through their distinct checking routes. (b) Loop-minus-execute/fix score difference $\Delta\phi$. Stripping commentary with categories fixed removes the positive separation. Bars are the archived 95\% paired-bootstrap intervals at resample size 100, seed 20260804 and 100 resamples. No interval was reported for the re-binned point. Formula-text scoring, program correctness and unequal search protocols prevent a causal recursion claim.}
\label{fig:dd-superarc-controls}
\end{figure}

The actual scored object requires care. Complexity was computed from formula text, not simply from the executable program retained beside it. Bare-arm correctness used scorer-side translation. The other arms used their banked programs, with an additional translation cross-check that did not always agree or succeed. This distinction matters because the scoring representation and the executable witness can otherwise appear to be the same object. The campaign preserved enough of both to expose the mismatch.

The adversarial follow-up found a direct confound. Commentary was much more common in loop answers, and the normalised text-complexity calculation could reward that extra text without adding generative information. Stripping commentary while holding answer categories fixed removes the positive loop-minus-execute/fix separation, as Figure~\ref{fig:dd-superarc-controls} shows. Reclassifying the stripped answers is a different protocol and gives a different point estimate. The apparent advantage was therefore sensitive to the representation being scored.

This correction is the campaign's most informative outcome. The system built an instrument, generated and executed candidates, preserved a frozen result, tested competing explanations and revised the interpretation. Unequal prompts and search access still require a controlled follow-up to isolate the effect of execution feedback. The demonstrated capacity is sustained research that leaves its conclusions open to inspection and correction.\footnote{\href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=reading\%2Fsuperarc-score-object-and-figure-provenance-20261015.md&expected_sha256=517aa07cdec80901c90ca09cb95dcefd7eb7f9e33ba7b01f2de8518658d3b607&owner=writing-artifact}{Exact scored object, frozen report pointers, format-control estimates and replot provenance}. \href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=reading\%2Foriginal-superarc-primary-and-campaign-comparison-20261015.md&expected_sha256=3c69c29e85f05b9c931f3532bc40334fae4a45b80ebce8c4f96aa44e3789c0eb&owner=writing-artifact}{Original primary paper and campaign comparison}.}

The same process can be applied to the system's own explanation. A book describing the present research environment was written and revised using that environment: \href{/projection/pdf?corpus=writing-system-architecture&file=synthetics+papers\%2Fwriting-system-architecture\%2Fmanuscript\%2FThe-writing-system-as-constituted-implementation-design-principles-and-outstanding-issues.pdf&expected_content_revision=sha256\%3Abfb748705add663891057b3c462363e0a7af3d73d3194992ab2b4c872ff66886}{The Living System Guide (PDF)}. It explains the objects, tools, human decisions and recoverable work described above. Writing it therefore tested whether the system could use its own evidence to make its operation clearer.

One example concerned the effect of changing a source. Several claims used that source, and a further conclusion drew those claims together. The book's diagram needed to distinguish a change in the supporting material from a change in the conclusion's actual wording. Inspection of the implemented behaviour exposed where the explanation blurred those two things, and the caption was corrected. The useful outcome was a clearer account of when a reader should reconsider a conclusion even though its sentence has not changed.

The book also had to work for someone who had not built the system. An independent reader identified passages and figures that were difficult to follow. Those findings led to revisions, a rebuilt book and a focused reread. That cycle connects a technical construction to a usable explanation: the reader's difficulty becomes a concrete revision, whose source and rendered outcome remain inspectable.\footnote{\href{/research/artifact?project=eigen-technical-due-diligence-briefing&scope=project&path=development\%2Fguide-and-dd-transition-evidence-20261016.json&expected_sha256=06906634ef890725a964c0eeb0679af955e8fa5cf91567f4e153677bc93945d2&owner=writing-artifact&artifact_id=ART-b9e10cb66439416894133c2a0622888c}{Primary correction, fixture checks, exact reader-acceptance scope and edition coordinates}.}

A larger theoretical argument tests a different use of the same infrastructure. \href{/projection/pdf?corpus=synthetics-foundations&file=synthetics+papers\%2Fsynthetics-foundations\%2Fmanuscript\%2FSynthetics-Foundations.pdf&expected_content_revision=sha256\%3A7be6d22efea797d5907b03f42086cb90e216adb5422d327a16bc012b84389dfa}{Foundations of Synthetics (PDF)}, the work from which the retained-state, residual and refinement constructions in this brief were drawn, develops its argument through linked derivations, finite examples and explanatory figures. Those pieces retain their claims, evidence and revision history, so they can be extended and inspected separately while the manuscript explains how they fit together. The demonstration is the construction and maintenance of a connected argument, alongside the individual mathematical results it contains.

The three demonstrations now form a progression: investigate a benchmark, improve the system's own explanation, and build a larger theoretical account from inspectable parts. Each leaves material that can support the next piece of work. This is the practical basis of guided self-improvement: an agent helps build and test a capability, while an author sets its direction and acceptance conditions. To make that capacity useful beyond these projects, the same objects and operations must become understandable and extensible to another developer.

\section{From a working core to an extensible SDK}
\label{section:from-a-working-core-to-an-extensible-sdk}

The route from these demonstrations to a reusable product is to expose the working core independently of this particular editor. Its organising unit is the object introduced above: an envelope carrying material, meaning and the grounds for using it. Such objects can be nested or linked without losing access to their detail. A result belongs to a calculation task, that task contributes to a comparison, and the comparison contributes to the project. Each level can expose a concise account while retaining a route to its detailed grounds. The \emph{altitude of a task} is the level at which its decision is being made: choosing a research direction, checking a calculation and editing a sentence need different observations of the same underlying work.

Figure~\ref{fig:dd-nested-work-sdk} follows this pattern through a parent task, a worker and an independent reviewer. The parent asks a bounded question and supplies the relevant context. The worker reads the necessary sources or runs the declared calculation, then returns a contribution with its evidence. The reviewer inspects that exact contribution. The parent consumes both the result and the review before deciding what belongs in the larger account. Context descends with the question, while observations and findings return with a known scope.

The current Work mechanism already distinguishes nesting from dependence. A containing goal contributes to the scope of its child tasks. A prerequisite relation specifies which completed contribution a later task relies on. Changing the parent goal can therefore change a child's scope, while changing an accepted prerequisite can require a consumer's acceptance to be reconsidered. This gives composed work an explicit basis at each level instead of treating the word \emph{done} as a timeless property. Historical completions remain recorded, while missing evidence about what they depended on remains visible.~\cite{Reference25a6c0}

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/robot-run-c4d4b3872a904ec0.result/dd-nested-work-sdk.pdf}
\caption{Composition across task altitudes. The parent sends a scoped question to a worker, receives an evidence-bearing contribution and consumes independent findings. Source, result and claim remain addressable within the child task. The amber marker on the neighbouring object shows where a changed input creates local review work. The dashed panel identifies the next SDK capabilities, using the same object and boundary vocabulary.}
\label{fig:dd-nested-work-sdk}
\end{figure}

Tools compose through the same discipline. One operation returns an identified result and the exact routes for inspecting or using it. The next operation consumes that result under its own conditions. A figure renderer, a claim-binding operation and a manuscript editor can therefore cooperate without sharing a hidden conversational memory. Their interfaces preserve the identity and meaning needed at the join.

The present system supplies the specialised objects, guarded tools, parent/worker/reviewer roles, bounded context and recorded acceptance used in this account. The next step is to package that working pattern as a standalone SDK. Its object templates should carry a description of their transitionable states, allowed operations, dependency effects and checks. Its extension instructions should travel with the code, so a developer can discover how a new capability fits rather than reconstructing the author's history.

A small extension makes the requirement tangible. An analysis module should declare its input types and revisions, output format, resource limits and failure behaviour. A result it produces should expose its interpretation and limitations, bind to the relevant claim and say which consumers need attention when an input changes. A new client should be able to inspect that result, propose a change and recover an interrupted operation through the same interfaces as the Writing App. The conformance examples should include successful use, a stale input, a repeated request and an attempted change outside the caller's authority.

This leads towards an operating environment for structured knowledge and agent work. An editor presents paragraphs and figures. A laboratory client presents samples and measurements. A research agent receives the objects needed for its task. A future frontend can let the author configure the topology and roles of a session network: which tasks run independently, which wait for evidence, who reviews them and where acceptance returns. The underlying contracts give those different interfaces a common meaning of identity, state and completion.

Source code can eventually become material inside this same structure. A kernel module can carry its purpose, dependencies, tests and allowed change process, just as a scientific claim carries its statement and grounds. A proposed code improvement would then be linked to the behaviour it intends to change, the checks it must pass and the review that admits it. This is the route to guided, traceable self-improvement: a useful increment increases the capacity available to build and inspect the next one.

The recursion matters because the same questions recur at each scale. What does this object retain? Which operation may change it? What does the change affect? What evidence makes the result usable? The SDK should make those questions answerable from its own interfaces and examples. A clean-environment test with an unfamiliar developer - one new result type, one second client, one interrupted operation recovered - would show whether the pattern has become a product that other people can extend.
